Schema, RLS, and triggers are defined in `docs/DATA_MODEL.md`; do not change schema without updating it.

Rules:
- Use relational Supabase tables; do not create one giant product JSON object.
- RLS sequencing: enable RLS at table create (deny-by-default). Task 12 adds published-product catalog policies and owner-only `user_ratings` policies (INSERT/UPDATE also require `is_published`), then client `GRANT`s. Anonymous reads are limited to `is_published` products and their related rows.
- Client write grants are column-level: `profiles` UPDATE only mutable profile fields (no client INSERT — rows come from `handle_new_user` on `auth.users`); `user_ratings` INSERT/UPDATE only scores + `private_note` (not `id` / timestamps). `updated_at` is trigger-maintained. Do not use PostgREST upsert of identity columns for ratings.
- Trusted Community Score recalculation happens in `refresh_rating_aggregates` (trigger/function) or equivalent server-side logic, never only on the client; revoke client `EXECUTE` on those helpers. Serialize refreshes per product before reading `user_ratings`. Ensure a zero-count aggregate row on product create.
- Never expose service-role keys in client code.
- Never access or write production databases from agents or MCP.

Schema, RLS, migration, and contract work follows the routine in `skills/supabase-schema-change/SKILL.md`.
